<title>USA: Dow Jones loses jury verdict in libel case.</title>
<headline>Dow Jones loses jury verdict in libel case.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal jury on Thursday awarded $222.7 million in damages to principals in a now-defunct securities firm in a libel suit against Dow Jones &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The jury's verdict followed a two-week long trial in which MMAR Group Inc said it had been forced out of business in 1993 following a critical article published in Dow Jones' Wall Street Journal.</p>
<p>Attorneys for Dow Jones said they planned to appeal.</p>
</text>
